On 06/24/2015 02:50 PM, Julie Bodin wrote:
> 1)When the model runs with two ordinal variables (R3AQ573 and R3AQ575),

> the following error message appear :
>
> Error in muthen1984(Data = X[[g]], ov.names = ov.names[[g]], ov.types =
> ov.types,:
>
> unknown ov.types:factor

At least one of the variables your model is declared as 'factor' (not
ordered!). lavaan can not handle this (yet). If it is a dependent
variable, you must declare it as ordered (if this makes sense).

> 2)Moreover, I have a problem with an exogenous categorical variable with

> 5 levels. In the previous model, I treat it as a binary variable
> (Part5cl_PCS_2Cl).
>
> I created 4 dummy (0/1) variables. However some estimated variances are
> negative.

Creating 4 dummy variables was the right way. That, after entering these
dummy variables in the model, some of the (residual?) variances become
negative, is a symptom that the model does not fit well.

Yves.

