I do have a model with 4 exogenous predictors on 4 endogenous DVs. In the second step I am analyzing the influence of those 4 endogenous DVs on to a binary outcome (0|1). Since lavaan can only handle probit regression with WLSMV yet and I really don´t want to use WLSMV (see my argument here <https://groups.google.com/forum/#!searchin/lavaan/logistic$20regression/lavaan/9wN4Z9pZ4ow/Rfnloue6QIsJ>) I try to predict latent factor scores (I know it´s actually a bad idea!) and use these factor scores for glm() . But I just saw today that the influence of the predictors on the DVs is not "out partialled" in the factor scores of the endogenous DVs. Is there any way of obtaining factor scores for the four DVs while controlling for the four predictors' influence on the DVs?

Thanks a lot!

PS: Yves, any news on logistic regression and MLR?

